## Why Almond Nails Are Still the Shape Everyone's Booking in 2026

Nail shape trends move slowly. That's the thing most trend roundups forget to say. The coffin boom lasted years. Stiletto had its moment and retreated to a niche. Almond, though, has done something different it's evolved rather than peaked. The shape flatters nearly every hand, photographs beautifully, and sits at the precise midpoint between elegant and practical that most women actually want from a manicure.

What's changed in 2026 is the *version* of almond people are requesting. The exaggerated, pointed almond of a few years ago has softened. The modern iteration is slightly shorter, rounder at the tip, with a taper that reads refined rather than dramatic. Nail artists are calling it the "soft almond" and it's the canvas every major trend this year is being built on.

