## What Is the Modern Almond Shape and Why Everyone's Asking for It?

The "modern almond" is a specific request that's been gaining traction on NailTok since late 2025. It describes an almond with a slightly squarer base more structure at the sidewall that tapers to a softer, less pointed tip than a traditional almond. The effect is architectural without being angular. It reads longer than an oval but less aggressive than a classic almond.

At the other end of the length spectrum, the micro almond is having its own moment. Think: almond shape on a genuinely short nail bed, with the taper starting almost immediately at the free edge. It's the practical answer for nail-conscious women who work with their hands, type all day, or simply prefer shorter nails. The shape still elongates. It still reads polished. It just doesn't require length to do so. <a href='/blog/short-almond-nails'>Short almond nails are having a major moment right now</a> and the micro almond is the most wearable version of that trend.

