## French Tip Almond Nails in 2026: Micro Lines, Colour Tips, and the Glasswing Effect

The French tip has been quietly dismantled and rebuilt from the ground up over the past eighteen months. What's emerged in 2026 is three distinct directions, all running at the same time.

The micro-French a tip line so fine it reads more as a suggestion than a statement is the most versatile and the most requested. It works on natural, gel, and BIAB builds and pairs with any base shade. Colour tips have replaced white as the adventurous option: sage, dusty rose, mocha, and ice blue are the shades appearing most frequently. And the glasswing effect, a near-invisible sheer tip that catches the light differently from the base, is the most technically demanding of the three but produces the most editorial result.

