## The Almond Nail Trends That Are Already Fading (So You Don't Waste a Salon Visit)

Mirror chrome. Heavy holographic glitter. Extremely long almond extensions that curve toward stiletto territory. Thick, high-contrast French lines with a stark white tip against a deep base. Chunky rhinestone clusters placed without restraint. These are the looks that were having their moment in 2024 and early 2025, and they're now past the point of feeling current.

None of this means you can't wear them personal taste is always the final word. But if you're specifically chasing what's *in* right now rather than what you personally love, these directions won't serve that goal. The <a href='https://www.nailsmag.com/industry-news' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>NAILS Magazine</a> industry conversation has shifted firmly toward refinement and finish quality over maximalist decoration, and that shift is visible across salon request data for 2026.

The specific tells that date a manicure in 2026: harsh contrast, obvious shine, and scale that competes with clothing rather than complements it.

